# Copy to .env.local and fill in. Both values are public identifiers that get
# inlined into the built output — neither is a secret. Leave a value blank to
# omit the corresponding tags entirely.

# GA4 measurement ID. This is the same "G-" ID that appears as `measurementId`
# in a Firebase web config: Firebase Analytics for web is GA4, so events land
# in the same property either way — there is no need to install the `firebase`
# package for analytics alone.
#
# Required at BUILD time (Vite inlines it), so it must be present wherever
# `npm run build` runs, not just where the Worker is deployed.
#
# Analytics is additionally gated at run time to the production host, so a
# build carrying this ID still reports nothing from dev or preview.
VITE_GA_MEASUREMENT_ID=

# Only needed if verifying Search Console by HTML tag. Prefer DNS TXT
# verification, or drop Google's googleXXXX.html file into public/ — both
# cover the client-rendered homepage, which this tag does not.
VITE_GOOGLE_SITE_VERIFICATION=
